WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.267
A docstring documents the purpose of a function.

00:00:03.267 --> 00:00:08.872
The triple-quoted text says that average returns the arithmetic mean of two numbers.

00:00:08.872 --> 00:00:15.492
That description becomes part of the function’s built-in documentation and can be accessed through average dot

00:00:15.492 --> 00:00:18.943
underscore underscore doc underscore underscore.

00:00:19.871 --> 00:00:27.258
Good documentation is especially useful when code will be reused by other people—or by you several months later.

00:00:27.258 --> 00:00:31.874
Try rewriting the docstring in your own words while keeping the meaning accurate.
